{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1449054-creating-a-summoner-v20","id":1449054,"title":"Creating a Summoner - V20","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-05-19T15:24:22-07:00","id":1449054,"title":"Creating a Summoner - V20","content":"Hi there,<br /> <br /> Any Ideas for creating a something like a Summoner?<br /> I am not talking about the Lasombra-Hentai-Tantacle-build, but more like necromancy path of bones (?) ***, Lord of the undead (maybe a mistranslation, I do not own the english v20).<br /> But what could be an alternative? I can think of Thaumaturgy, &quot;Elemental Master&quot;.<br /> Any other Ideas for a Character which would prefer to let something like &quot;pets&quot; fight?<br /> <br /> Have a nice day &amp; thank you for reading!<br /> <br /> Edit: I am the ST and open to use uncommon Bloodlines or disciplines, as long as they got rules (or crossover with other splats).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26522,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26522-quin_shihuangdi","user":"Quin_Shihuangdi","date":". 05-19-2021, 06:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26522-quin_shihuangdi","name":"Quin_Shihuangdi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-19T22:09:23-07:00","id":1449089,"title":"","content":"Most obvious choice is to use Animalism; prime the animals with feral whispers to fight for you, perhaps ghoul them, and then call them when needed. But if you really must use &quot;magic&quot; there's the path of Conjuring 5 (perhaps you could make robots with 3)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-20T00:01:29-07:00","id":1449096,"title":"","content":"There are a few different ways to do the summoner style of play with vampire.<br /> <br /> As MyWifeisScary mentioned, Animalism makes for an easy starting point, though for maximum benefit it should be Nosferatu summoner since their vitae causes fun mutations in the animals, not to mention by being sewer focused, you have a way to move your occasionally giant critters around a city without them being seen by way of the tunnels. Eventually when Obfuscate gets high enough you can always have the critters with you while invisible.<br /> <br /> Thaumaturgy has several options, some xp cheap and some insanely xp expensive to build.<br /> <br /> The Green Path at rank three &amp; five basically allows you to turn nearby plants into minions. But this requires plants to be present and of sufficient size to do anything.<br /> <br /> The Elemental Mastery path allows the same thing with inanimate objects. This works better in a city environment since there are so many things that can animated.<br /> <br /> The Path of Technomancy has some interesting applications for drone technology, but that is getting more cyberpunk than some would like.<br /> <br /> Or if you want to absolutely go ham on the concept and don't care about XP costs, you run a Dominate 5 &amp; Path of Conjuring 5 Tremere with high combat stats and a background in chemistry. You use Path of Conjuring to create a body double of yourself (this is a mortal non-vampiric body as per the path power), you then use Dominate 5 to Possess the body double. You now can go on suicide missions or fight to the very end as you please, as long as you choose to leave the body before death occurs. The path of conjuring also means you can create what ever guns, ammo, or explosives you may want for the combat run. The inspiration for this came from the Altered Carbon series on Netflix, essentially the Tremere is a &quot;combat sleeve&quot; specialist. Add high level Auspex to the mix and things get really crazy with this build.<br /> <br /> Necromancy is an interesting summoner concept, but mostly because it requires a bit more thought that the other methods.<br /> <br /> The Sepulchre Path is straight forward with soul binding. The benefit is that few clans can counter a ghost or specter and thus this is potentially very powerful. The down side of this is that mortals and other creatures don't automatically become ghosts, so it is up to the ST if you can even find a ghost to bind to your service and even then, there is no way to ensure it is a useful ghost. A ghost librarian might be good for research, but generally useless in combat.<br /> <br /> The Bone Path allows you to make zombie minions, but once again this is a tricky thing. You need corpses laying about to use the power and the walking dead tend to be considered a masquerade violation. On the other hand if you dress all your zombies in full length clothes and masks, no one will be the wiser. I have had more use for the bone path during clean up where you have the corpses more or less clean up their own murder and then march into a vehicle.<br /> <br /> If you want a bit more specialized minions, rather than hordes, then I would suggest a Tzimisce who has a few fleshcrafted animal ghouls inside them. This combines their Animalism and Vicissitude abilities. A couple of football sized spider ghouls emerging from flesh crafted nests in the abdomen and attacking the vampires enemies is sure provide some shock factor. Ghoul Leeches that are two or three feet long with potence and flesh crafted stats can emerge from plenty of places.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-20T08:35:25-07:00","id":1449117,"title":"","content":"Thank you very, very much!<br /> <br /> The tzimisce sounds very interesting...<br /> Anyhow, ever since I had trouble to imagine the right usage of ghost/wraith. Maybe because it is the splat, which I never owned the rules to.<br /> So, how would a summoned wraith fight? Is it only rolling dices without a chance to fight back?<br /> Accordingly, bone path offers to bind a soul through demonic possession - could you bind it in a body build for fighting? <br /> <br /> And, again, thank you very much! I really appreciate the Ideas!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26522-quin_shihuangdi","name":"Quin_Shihuangdi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-20T13:51:30-07:00","id":1449140,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Quin_Shihuangdi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1449054-creating-a-summoner-v20?p=1449117#post1449117\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thank you very, very much!<br /> <br /> The tzimisce sounds very interesting...<br /> Anyhow, ever since I had trouble to imagine the right usage of ghost/wraith. Maybe because it is the splat, which I never owned the rules to.<br /> <b>So, how would a summoned wraith fight?</b> Is it only rolling dices without a chance to fight back?<br /> Accordingly, bone path offers to bind a soul through demonic possession - could you bind it in a body build for fighting?<br /> <br /> And, again, thank you very much! I really appreciate the Ideas!</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't get much opportunity to play wraith, so my information may need double-checking, but off the top of my head from Wraith20:<br /> <br /> Wraiths can interact directly with the skinlands (the living world) through what's called embodiment (physically manifesting) or by puppetry/skinriding (possessing a host (vampires are also vulnerable)). In this state, disciplines affect them as they would a human.<br /> <br /> Whilst they're there, your wraith minions can:<ul><li>Damage a target so badly it falls into Oblivion, erasing them/it from existence. (But it's a 5 dot ability, good luck enslaving a wraith with this power without having your soul annihilated, let alone finding one with this power in the first place.)</li> <li>Rip souls out of their bodies. Create illusions and control dreams.</li> <li>Engage in poltergeist activity. Throw things around, stake vampires, decapitate vampires, hit things with raw force and inflict damage, oh, and they can<i> set things on fire</i>. Including a vampire's clothes or hair...</li> <li>Embody themselves so that they're only perceived by specific people.</li> <li>They can restore blood and health. Or steal it.</li> <li>Wreck celerity by messing with the flow of time.</li> <li>See into the past and future.</li> <li>Manipulate emotions around them, which includes driving vampires into or out of frenzy,</li> <li>While skinriding a host they appear to be the person they're possessing. They can infiltrate as spies, frame people and, yes, physically attack using these bodies, so on so forth</li> <li>They can interfere with dominate by possessing a dominated target if you want to mess up somebody's plan, but this involves a battle of wills between the wraith and vampire for control of the host.</li> <li>And they can do a banshee scream that counts as a physical attack.</li> </ul>Supernaturals have a better chance of realising that something happening and fighting against possession and mind control better than mortals, but they're not immune. And they can't do anything about powers that don't directly target them like time-control or immolation.<br /> <br /> I'd advise browsing the Arcanoi on the wiki for ideas or something.<br /> <br /> There's no reason you can't use daemonic posession to put a wraith into a recently dead soldier's corpse or something. Pretty sure they benefit from the combat skills and such","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><sup><i>Prone to hyperbole</i></sup>","edited":{"userid":26836,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","user":"Rhywbeth","date":". 05-20-2021, 08:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","name":"Rhywbeth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26836_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"377"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-20T14:12:26-07:00","id":1449143,"title":"","content":"I think I would go for the Sepulchre Path if you want wraith minions using their powers for you.<br /> The Bone Path can give you zombie minions, but zombies aren't as versatile as wraiths. On the other hand, they're more readily obedient, emotionally stable, need less convincing/threatening, and are less prone to vengeance and/or turning into insane evil minions in service of the universal concept of entropy seeking to devour existence<br /> <br /> Wraiths are also rare and the powerful ones are usually the ones that don't have fetters to blackmail them with, as far as I remember. There's no guarantee a wraith has the abilities you need (although you could start a wraith farm I guess. Enslave wraiths and have them develop their powers, have them hunt down the newly dead and train them...)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><sup><i>Prone to hyperbole</i></sup>","edited":{"userid":26836,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","user":"Rhywbeth","date":". 05-20-2021, 05:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","name":"Rhywbeth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26836_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"377"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}